<title>USA: U.S. cotton weekly export sales highlights - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. cotton weekly export sales highlights - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA cotton export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Net Upland sales of 85,900 running bales (RB) were off 41 percent from the previous week and 36 percent from the 4-week average.  The major increases were for Mexico (30,200 RB), China (22,100 RB), and Venezuela (15,000 RB).</p>
<p>Exports of 180,200 RB were 28 percent less than the previous week's marketing-year high and 11 percent below the 4-week average.  Asian destinations accounted for 58 percent of the week's shipments; Western Hemisphere, 32 percent; and West European, 10 percent.</p>
</text>
